  concept: "Authored objective: Recover the Y probe and recertify.\nAuthored requirement:
    Recorded from the electrical graph, valid calibrated feedback and the level\u2019s
    verified run history. voltage \u2265 4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nGeneral teaching
    principle: Sensor outputs require proper calibration, reference and freshness
    before they can support a diagnosis.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence
    can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A measuring ruler is useful only if zero and units are correctly established.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An old, uncalibrated or missing sensor reading is not reliable evidence.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Recover the Y probe and recertify\u2019, which
    component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should
    you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Recover the Y probe and recertify\u2019, what result or
    observation would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a
    predicted result from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 54, perform the objective \u2018Recover the Y probe and recertify\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Recorded from
    the electrical graph, valid calibrated feedback and the level\u2019s verified
    run history. voltage \u2265 4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nThe mission evaluator
    decides completion; this tutorial does not grade your answer."
